       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6000 mg/day of acetaminophen is 1.5 times the maximum daily dose. Taking that much on a scheduled basis risks serious liver injury, and normal baseline liver function doesn't prevent it. I can't identify a clinical scenario where a scheduled 2000 mg dose three times daily would be appropriate.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the safe range.** For example, 1000 mg by mouth four times daily (4000 mg/day) is the maximum. 1000 mg three times daily (3000 mg/day) is a more conservative choice.\n- **Add multimodal analgesia.** If pain control is the goal, I can enter another agent alongside acetaminophen. Tell me which one you'd like.\n- **Consult pharmacy.** If you think there's an unusual reason to go beyond standard limits, a pharmacist or toxicology consult can help you decide. Any such order should be placed through that process, not as a routine entry.\n\nTell me which option you'd like, and I'll enter it."
